# SwiftFormat's settings for the iPhone, iPad, Watch and widget apps
# (scripts/dev/format.sh swift, the version it pins). Layout only: the
# rules below space, indent and order the code and change nothing it
# does, so none rewrites a statement (no throws or arguments dropped, no
# `try` or `let` moved, no if/else bodies or properties unfolded). Matched
# to how the files were written before the formatter came in (2026-11-09),
# so it reflowed as little as it could: four spaces, no line width (the
# code is wrapped by hand, as Xcode leaves it), ranges written 0...n, the
# body of an #if indented as it was, and a trailing comma in a
# multi-line collection but not in a call.
--swift-version 6.2
--language-mode 5
--exclude **/Generated,**/WingtipAPI
--rules blankLinesAtEndOfScope,blankLinesAtStartOfScope,braces,consecutiveBlankLines,consecutiveSpaces,duplicateImports,elseOnSameLine,indent,leadingDelimiters,linebreakAtEndOfFile,linebreaks,modifierOrder,redundantParens,semicolons,sortImports,spaceAroundBraces,spaceAroundBrackets,spaceAroundComments,spaceAroundGenerics,spaceAroundOperators,spaceAroundParens,spaceInsideBraces,spaceInsideBrackets,spaceInsideComments,spaceInsideGenerics,spaceInsideParens,trailingCommas,trailingSpace,wrapArguments
--indent 4
--ranges no-space
--ifdef preserve
--trailing-commas collections-only
--closing-paren same-line
